📖 Book Note

To insert a node before the tail of a DLL, first handle the empty and single-node cases. If there is one node, the new node becomes the new head and is connected before the old head/tail. Otherwise, traverse to the tail and insert the new node between tail.prev and tail by updating four links: newNode.next, newNode.prev, tail.prev.next, and tail.prev.

Time: O(n)
Auxiliary Space: O(1)




class Solution {
    public ListNode insertBeforeTail(ListNode head, int X) {

        // Create the new node.
        ListNode newNode = new ListNode(X);

        // If the list is empty, there is no tail.
        if (head == null) {
            return newNode;
        }

        // If there is only one node,
        // that node is both head and tail.
        if (head.next == null) {

            // New node comes before the old head/tail.
            newNode.next = head;

            // Old head/tail points back to new node.
            head.prev = newNode;

            // New node becomes the new head.
            return newNode;
        }

        // Start from head and move to the tail.
        ListNode current = head;

        while (current.next != null) {
            current = current.next;
        }

        // current is now the old tail.
        // The new node should come before current.
        newNode.next = current;

        // The new node's previous node is
        // the node that was before the old tail.
        newNode.prev = current.prev;

        // Connect the previous node forward to newNode.
        current.prev.next = newNode;

        // Connect the old tail backward to newNode.
        current.prev = newNode;

        // Head has not changed for a multi-node list.
        return head;
    }
}
